  "solution": {
    "text": "The angular momentum of an electron in an <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit is given by<br /><math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>m</mtext>   <mtext>e</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>vr</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>n</mtext><mo>&#x22C5;</mo><mfrac>   <mtext>h</mtext>   <mrow>    <mtext>2&#x03C0;</mtext></mrow>  </mfrac>  <mo>;</mo><mtext>n</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2.3.......</mn></mrow></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>13.6</mn><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br />Potential energy <math><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>13.6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Potential energy <math><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>13.6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>∵</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathv